Subject: [PATCH] Stabilise drag: hysteresis, NMS, global tracking, smoothing

Four defects cause window jitter during slow touch drags on the 3200x2136
panel (sensor grid ~40x60, one cell ~53 px):

1. No hysteresis — find_points() uses a fixed threshold; a stationary
   finger's capacitance blob oscillates across it, producing repeated
   lift/repress events.
2. No non-maximum suppression — one finger can leave two adjacent 3x3
   maxima, creating a ghost contact that competes for the drag.
3. Per-slot greedy matching in track() — two crossing fingers swap slots,
   handing the drag to the wrong finger for multiple frames.
4. ui_report() binds ABS_X/ABS_Y to the lowest-numbered active slot
   instead of the longest-held contact; the compositor's pointer
   emulation follows the wrong finger.

Fixes:
- Tracked contacts stay alive at threshold/2 within PEAK_HOLD_CELLS (2).
- Candidates sorted by peak strength; weaker peaks within PEAK_MIN_DIST
  (2 cells ~107 px) are suppressed.
- track() uses iterative global-minimum pairing (no slot swap).
- New slot_move(): 8.8 fixed-point low-pass (SMOOTH_ALPHA=96/256) with
  snap bypass above SMOOTH_SNAP_DIST (24 px).
- ui_report() ABS_X/ABS_Y follows the slot with the greatest age.

Tuning knobs are the four macros at the top of the file.  Threshold
default, report rate, coordinate transform and pen decode are unchanged.

